I need some spices for cooking.
I go into a small shop.
The shop has a good smell.
There are many items in open sacks there.
The shopkeeper is standing there.
"I need a hundred grams of black pepper and a hundred grams of cardamom," I say.
He weighs it on a scale.
Then he wraps it in paper.
"How much is the total?" I ask.
"It is two hundred and sixty rupees," he says.
I take my purse.
He waves his hand.
"Give me two hundred and fifty rupees," he says.
Smiling, I give him the money.
He gives me those packets.
I put them in my bag.
